Sibling of #1, on the other transport. lib/Net/Async/MCP/Server/Transport/StreamableHTTP.pm, listen(): binds via HTTP::Server::PSGI and runs its own accept loop, so nothing else in the IO::Async loop gets a turn while the server is up. Its POD already calls this out and calls a real async bring-up a future ticket - this is that ticket, so the note has something to point at.

Its POD cross-reference was corrected as part of #1: it used to claim the same caveat applied to Stdio/handle_requests, which is no longer true.

A real fix is an IO::Async::Listener (or IO::Async::Loop::listen) accepting into IO::Async::Stream connections with an HTTP parser, rather than HTTP::Server::PSGI driving the process. That is a larger change than #1 was and needs a decision on whether the Plack/PSGI app interface (to_app) stays the primary entry point, with listen() as the convenience wrapper.

